    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">8. Tax revenue</narrative>
    </title>
    <baseline iso-date="2016-12-30" value="13.50" year="2016"></baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2016-12-30"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2019-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="14.90">
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&amp;gt;Not achieved.The indicator for this component was &amp;lsquo;tax revenue as a percentage of GDP&amp;rsquo; with a revised baseline of 13.5 percent (2016) and a target of 14.9 percent (end-2019), translating to a significant 1.4 percentage point increase. However, while the actual achieved in 2018 was 15.2 percent, which was above the target, the 2019 actual fell back to 14.3 percent.&amp;nbsp;The improvement is still not discouraging given that the government had to absorb some fiscal costs related to the program.&amp;nbsp; For example, it was costly to the government to convert NIGELEC&amp;rsquo;s debt to equity, and &amp;nbsp;the provision of tax incentives to the telecom sector, which was estimated to lead to 0.4 percent of GDP foregone revenue, and transfers of the mining revenue arrears to communes, all of which were financed through the budget. Though these reforms are net beneficial in the long-term, they made somewhat more challenging to reach the revenue target.&lt;/p&amp;gt;

&lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&amp;gt;

&lt;p&amp;gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&amp;gt;</narrative>
      </comment>
